{"author":{"id":"2de4467f26c42fb223f4d3ddd5611e7c0513d3daae4c1dc315de039036bc997d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778952265,"nonce":"7l69GC2heAJPRTEOsZQ0aJLBMcg=","title":"Fix nested margin-note directives inside note scopes","message":"## Problem\nNested directive conversion is breaking positioned margin notes. `:::margin-note` inside `::::note-scope` renders as ordinary block content instead of a `MarginNote` component, so target positioning and mobile/desktop note behavior never run.\n\nObserved example: `content/posts/hashing-python-functions.md` has `:::margin-note{target=\\\"PyTree\\\"}` inside a note scope, but the built DOM contains a plain `\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e...\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e` under `.note-scope` rather than a `.marginnote` element.\n\n## Context\nThe directive transformer returns `SKIP` after converting a container directive, which prevents traversal into nested directive children. The later `remark-sidenotes` pass expects nested `MarginNote` JSX nodes to already exist.\n\nThis likely explains several historical margin-note/callout failures: the CSS and positioning logic are not always seeing the component tree it was designed for.\n\n## Potential Solutions\n- Make directive conversion recursive or bottom-up so nested directives are transformed before parent containers return.\n- Add render/regression tests for `note-scope` containing targeted margin notes, untargeted margin notes, code-block targets, and callout-contained notes.\n- After conversion works, simplify the note CSS/JS rather than patching around missing components.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}